<title>USA: Allegheny Airport $465 mln deal possible next week.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Airport $465 mln deal possible next week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $465 million Allegheny County Airport, Pa., refunding deal could price as early as next week, Gary Bishop, director of aviation, said.</p>
<p>&quot;We could go as early as next Wednesday or Thursday, or we may delay it a week,&quot; Bishop said, adding that the deal's timing will depend both on favorable market conditions and the progress of some legal processes within the county.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co is the bookrunner, while Goldman Sachs is the co-manager, he said.</p>
<p>--Kathie O'Donnell, 212-859-1655</p>
